Execute Phase 1 only.

GOAL
Code inside this app sends a real authenticated request to
Ollama Cloud and displays the actual final reply.

Use the server-side OLLAMA_API_KEY.
Never request the key in chat or expose it in frontend code.

IMPLEMENT
- A protected server endpoint for model testing.
- A simple authenticated connection-test screen.
- Server-side allowlisted model selection.
- Timeout, request-size limit, and bounded output.
- Safe error handling.
- No arbitrary upstream URL supplied by the browser.

Use:
POST https://ollama.com/api/chat

Start with:
{
  "model": "<verified-cloud-request-id>",
  "messages": [
    {"role": "user", "content": "Write one short welcome sentence for StoryFrame."}
  ],
  "stream": false
}

Set Authorization: Bearer using the server secret.

Verify the actual response structure.
Display the final message content, not hidden reasoning.

Do not call localhost:11434.
Do not substitute a fixture.

TEST ALL SIX FAMILIES
Resolve exact cloud identifiers from current docs/account access.
Make small sequential test calls within an approved test budget.

For each record:
- Requested model.
- Returned model where supplied.
- Success/failure.
- Final reply.
- Latency.
- Usage fields actually returned.
- Sanitized provider error if unavailable.

Do not silently substitute another model for Nemotron or GPT-OSS.

ACCEPTANCE
At least one real reply is displayed by the app.

This phase is fully complete only when all six have been tested
and their actual availability is reported.
Unavailable models remain disabled.

Show the real test replies in the completion report.
Never invent them.

Stop after Phase 1.
